Oh, and tell everyone downstairs from Modern Shogi to come up.

288
00:16:17,328 --> 00:16:21,028
Take all you can carry. How about it, Smith? 40 sardines.

289
00:16:21,028 --> 00:16:25,148
Are you serious? What's a bachelor gonna do with 40 fish?

290
00:16:25,528 --> 00:16:30,048
And what's with the teardrop sunglasses? You supposed to be some kind of old hipster?

291
00:16:30,188 --> 00:16:34,688
Never mind the fish, chairman. Just introduce me to a woman who will fillet the fish for me.

292
00:16:34,748 --> 00:16:35,128
Really?

293
00:16:35,468 --> 00:16:37,888
Ah, really? There's so much.

294
00:16:38,028 --> 00:16:38,528
Grand!

295
00:16:38,528 --> 00:16:43,308
Mr. Goto should have taken some home with him, since he's a married man and all.

296
00:16:43,788 --> 00:16:46,508
Yes, but his wife's still in the hospital. It's a shame.

297
00:16:46,828 --> 00:16:48,428
Huh? Oh, I see.

298
00:16:48,528 --> 00:16:51,908
Nakamura! Are these all the bags we have?

299
00:16:51,988 --> 00:16:53,148
I'll look for more!

300
00:16:53,148 --> 00:17:02,828
I guess I don't have a choice.

301
00:17:03,148 --> 00:17:05,348
I'll go ahead and take these bluish ones.

302
00:17:05,688 --> 00:17:06,628
What's it called again?

303
00:17:07,048 --> 00:17:08,248
DHA, wasn't it?

304
00:17:08,408 --> 00:17:10,748
From what I've heard, it's supposed to be good for the brain.

305
00:17:14,088 --> 00:17:15,448
Well, have a good evening.

306
00:17:16,248 --> 00:17:19,448
I'll eat this while coming up with some countermeasures against Goto.

307
00:17:19,448 --> 00:17:22,068
Yeah, I'd better head out, too.

308
00:17:23,148 --> 00:17:23,708
Kiriyawa!

309
00:17:23,948 --> 00:17:24,348
Yeah!

310
00:17:24,988 --> 00:17:28,228
Hmm. I've been talking to the owner of Bar Masaki.

311
00:17:28,848 --> 00:17:33,968
I hear you've been spending time at her beautiful niece's house and enjoying their hospitality lately.

312
00:17:34,548 --> 00:17:36,208
Please, I can't breathe, sir!

313
00:17:36,308 --> 00:17:38,168
You better keep that info to yourself.

314
00:17:38,888 --> 00:17:42,148
There are plenty of our associates who carry a torch for Akari.

315
00:17:42,608 --> 00:17:44,328
Get what I'm trying to say here, son?

316
00:17:47,068 --> 00:17:47,588
Heavy!

317
00:17:48,228 --> 00:17:48,708
Breathe!

318
00:17:48,708 --> 00:17:49,688
Ew, gross!

319
00:17:49,908 --> 00:17:51,228
Do you smell something fishy?

320
00:17:51,628 --> 00:17:54,548
If she's helping you out, why don't you take her some fish?

321
00:17:54,948 --> 00:17:57,268
The owner says she's a really good cook.

322
00:17:57,648 --> 00:17:58,128
Heavy!

323
00:17:58,968 --> 00:18:01,328
He loaded me up with so much fish.

324
00:18:02,088 --> 00:18:04,068
Fileting all of them is a lot of work.

325
00:18:04,508 --> 00:18:06,328
What if it ends up being a big burden to her?

326
00:18:10,708 --> 00:18:18,308
Whenever I'm here, I always feel so warm and welcomed.

327
00:18:18,308 --> 00:18:20,628
It's comfortable.

328
00:18:20,628 --> 00:18:20,668
It's comfortable.

329
00:18:20,728 --> 00:18:24,868
This house is like a warm kotatsu.

330
00:18:24,868 --> 00:18:28,708
I'm afraid I'll never be able to leave again.

331
00:18:29,668 --> 00:18:32,128
That's why I thought I should stay away for a while.

332
00:18:32,128 --> 00:18:35,508
But here I am again.

333
00:18:35,508 --> 00:18:48,788
I'll fillet the rock fish and fry up some fish sticks, and we can have that for lunch tomorrow.

334
00:18:48,788 --> 00:18:53,108
Then I can salt and dry the sardines and save them for pizza and pasta.

335
00:18:53,108 --> 00:18:57,088
Oh, then I'll fillet the flounder and split it into salted fish and sashimi.

336
00:18:57,088 --> 00:18:58,348
Okay, then.

337
00:18:58,488 --> 00:18:59,088
So that means...

338
00:18:59,708 --> 00:19:02,848
Imagine how much we'll save on our food bill!

339
00:19:03,528 --> 00:19:04,388
This is great!

340
00:19:04,728 --> 00:19:05,548
Thanks so much!

341
00:19:05,768 --> 00:19:06,248
Swish!

342
00:19:07,128 --> 00:19:11,188
We pulled out all the stops for New Year's, so we're a little low on our food money.

343
00:19:11,508 --> 00:19:13,868
But now we can have all kinds of delicious food again.

344
00:19:13,948 --> 00:19:14,648
This is great!

345
00:19:15,168 --> 00:19:15,928
Stand by!

346
00:19:16,088 --> 00:19:16,548
Okay!

347
00:19:16,688 --> 00:19:17,248
All ready!

348
00:19:17,248 --> 00:19:21,068
Miso soup with deep-fried tofu.

349
00:19:22,448 --> 00:19:23,948
Lotus root and carrots.

350
00:19:24,788 --> 00:19:26,628
Warm rice with a raw egg.

351
00:19:27,428 --> 00:19:29,708
We already finished with dinner earlier.

352
00:19:30,208 --> 00:19:32,068
They're just leftovers, but I hope it'll do.

353
00:19:33,528 --> 00:19:35,348
Sorry it isn't much, but enjoy!

354
00:19:42,188 --> 00:19:43,288
It's delicious!

355
00:19:43,928 --> 00:19:45,948
This egg rice is so good!

356
00:19:45,948 --> 00:19:48,688
What do you mean it isn't much?

357
00:19:49,048 --> 00:19:49,868
Piping hot!

358
00:19:49,948 --> 00:19:53,748
It's just rice topped with egg and soy sauce, but it's so good!

359
00:20:00,868 --> 00:20:03,328
I'm glad you finally got over your cold, Rei.

360
00:20:03,868 --> 00:20:05,908
Your voice sounds like it's back to normal again.

361
00:20:06,648 --> 00:20:09,368
Thank you for everything you did for me over the holidays.

362
00:20:09,868 --> 00:20:11,068
I appreciate it.

363
00:20:11,068 --> 00:20:14,328
Rei, Rei, stay here.

364
00:20:14,568 --> 00:20:16,708
I want you to snuggle with Mama tonight.

365
00:20:16,948 --> 00:20:17,948
What a great idea!

366
00:20:18,388 --> 00:20:20,108
Why don't we have a slumber party, Rei?

367
00:20:20,488 --> 00:20:21,328
And guess what?

368
00:20:21,528 --> 00:20:24,208
The lady next door gave us this really cool jigsaw puzzle.

369
00:20:24,448 --> 00:20:25,448
One thousand pieces!

370
00:20:25,788 --> 00:20:27,668
And we can put it together on the kotatsu!

371
00:20:27,668 --> 00:20:31,668
A home that's just like a warm kotatsu.

372
00:20:31,668 --> 00:20:32,668
This warmth...

373
00:20:32,668 --> 00:20:37,468
I can't.

374
00:20:37,688 --> 00:20:39,428
I have to go back to my place tonight.

375
00:20:39,768 --> 00:20:40,128
Huh?

376
00:20:40,188 --> 00:20:40,888
Why, Rei?

377
00:20:41,048 --> 00:20:42,728
Momo wants you to stay here!

378
00:20:43,228 --> 00:20:43,808
Why?

379
00:20:44,128 --> 00:20:45,068
Why, Rei?

380
00:20:45,468 --> 00:20:46,048
Why?

381
00:20:46,268 --> 00:20:46,708
Why?

382
00:20:46,708 --> 00:20:56,868
A home that's just like a warm kotatsu.

383
00:21:11,548 --> 00:21:12,148
Momo.

384
00:21:13,148 --> 00:21:14,188
I'm sorry.

385
00:21:14,188 --> 00:21:18,148
It's just, I've got a match coming up that I can't lose.

386
00:21:18,588 --> 00:21:19,228
It's important.

387
00:21:19,668 --> 00:21:22,088
I have to go home now so I can study and prepare.

388
00:21:22,608 --> 00:21:23,668
Study and prepare?

389
00:21:24,128 --> 00:21:25,328
Does Rei have a test?

390
00:21:25,928 --> 00:21:26,408
Yes.

391
00:21:27,248 --> 00:21:28,248
A big test.

392
00:21:28,928 --> 00:21:30,448
I have to show my opponent.

393
00:21:31,328 --> 00:21:32,348
I have what it takes.

394
00:21:32,908 --> 00:21:34,848
I've trained hard enough to make it this far.

395
00:21:41,688 --> 00:21:42,248
Mama.

396
00:21:43,148 --> 00:21:43,448
Huh?

397
00:21:44,188 --> 00:21:47,028
Don't you have something to say to Rei?

398
00:21:47,648 --> 00:21:48,328
To Rei?

399
00:21:49,108 --> 00:21:51,828
But Rei has a test and he has to study.

400
00:21:52,248 --> 00:21:52,628
Yeah.

401
00:21:52,948 --> 00:21:55,248
And what do we say when we want to support someone?

402
00:21:56,948 --> 00:21:59,048
Go tell him to do your best.

403
00:21:59,868 --> 00:22:00,208
Hmm?

404
00:22:04,548 --> 00:22:05,488
Listen, Rei.

405
00:22:05,908 --> 00:22:07,148
Do your best!

406
00:22:07,148 --> 00:22:07,208
Do your best!

407
00:22:11,208 --> 00:22:11,668
Right.

408
00:22:11,668 --> 00:22:16,728
You've got it.

409
00:22:20,728 --> 00:22:22,768
Smith is going up against Goto next.

410
00:22:23,308 --> 00:22:25,428
And my next opponent is Shimada.

411
00:22:26,508 --> 00:22:27,228
After that...

412
00:22:27,228 --> 00:22:29,228
Whoever winds up winning...

413
00:22:29,228 --> 00:22:32,648
...will head to the finals.

414
00:22:32,648 --> 00:22:41,248
The wind whistles, playing the chords on the bridge like a harp.

415
00:22:42,608 --> 00:22:46,028
There was nothing I could do the last time he beat me to a pulp.

416
00:22:46,988 --> 00:22:48,788
He was left without a scratch.

417
00:22:49,348 --> 00:22:51,148
I'll show him.

418
00:22:53,468 --> 00:22:56,068
You won't be his punching bag on the Shogi board.

419
00:22:57,828 --> 00:22:58,108
Yeah!

420
00:22:58,108 --> 00:22:58,488
No!

421
00:22:58,488 --> 00:22:59,068
I'll show him.

422
00:22:59,068 --> 00:23:00,128
I won't be his punching bag on the Shogi board.

423
00:23:00,128 --> 00:23:00,548
I won't be his punching bag on the Shogi board.

424
00:23:00,548 --> 00:23:30,528
Thank you.

425
00:24:31,011 --> 00:24:36,011
Ah, alright. Time to go.

426
00:24:36,011 --> 00:24:40,011
Yes. Well, I guess... there is something.

427
00:24:40,011 --> 00:24:44,011
I want you to crush Kiriyama's pride in your next Shogi match!

428
00:24:44,011 --> 00:24:47,011
Next time, be decisive.

429
00:24:47,011 --> 00:24:50,011
I can't believe it! Option C!

430
00:24:52,011 --> 00:24:54,011
March comes in like a lion.

431
00:24:54,011 --> 00:24:58,011
It's like you can't miss the next episode, you know?

432
00:25:02,011 --> 00:25:03,011
Mmm.

433
00:25:03,011 --> 00:25:07,011
Okay, sure...

434
00:25:07,011 --> 00:25:10,011
It's like you to be able to make a worry.

435
00:25:10,011 --> 00:25:14,011
As our forehead covers what the hands...

436
00:25:14,011 --> 00:25:16,011
I just Polarsi makes a big noise!

437
00:25:16,011 --> 00:25:21,011
So, as your forehead ouvertes, that's what intersecting the ties...

438
00:25:21,011 --> 00:25:23,011
So, try it.

439
00:25:23,011 --> 00:25:26,011
I want you to repose all the faces...

440
00:25:27,011 --> 00:25:30,011
So let me get it!

